      "content": "Here's a revised draft:\n\nSubject: Discrepancy in Last Month's Invoice\n\nDear [Supplier's Name],\n\nI am writing to bring to your attention an issue with our recent invoice for last month's resin delivery. Our records show that the total weight billed was 500kg more than what we actually received. This discrepancy is not an isolated incident, as we have experienced similar errors on previous occasions.\n\nWhile we understand that mistakes can happen, the cumulative effect of these errors is starting to impact our accounting team's workload and accuracy. We rely on accurate and timely invoices to manage our business operations, and we expect a higher level of quality from our suppliers.\n\nIn light of this, we would like to request a credit memo to adjust the balance accordingly. We would appreciate it if you could provide a revised invoice with the corrected weight and a detailed explanation for the discrepancy. We would also like to discuss ways to prevent such errors from occurring in the future.\n\nPlease let us know if there's any additional information you need from us to facilitate this process. We look forward to hearing back from you soon.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n\nThis revised draft is more direct and assertive, while still maintaining a professional tone. It clearly communicates your concerns",
